        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Initializes the test suite and creates test cases.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="remark"><para>RamWrite Writes <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> DWORDs of NOP methods into ordinary cached RAM. Baseline for the CPU&apos;s store throughput.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>PushbufferWrite Writes <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> DWORDs of NOP methods into the pushbuffer&apos;s memory without submitting them, so the GPU never reads them. Compared to RamWrite, shows the cost of writing to the pushbuffer&apos;s memory itself.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>PushbufferSubmit Writes <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> DWORDs of NOP methods directly into the pushbuffer and submits them with pbkit every 8K DWORDs, resetting the pushbuffer at the same points as Pushbuffer does. Compared to PushbufferWrite, shows the cost of the GPU consuming commands while the CPU is writing them.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>PushbufferAPI Pushes <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> DWORDs of NOP methods through Pushbuffer::Push with deferred submission, which submits and resets at the same points as PushbufferSubmit. Compared to PushbufferSubmit, shows the overhead of the Pushbuffer API.</para>
</simplesect>
Every test starts its frame with an empty pushbuffer, and any reset needed to return the pushbuffer to Pushbuffer&apos;s control happens after the frame&apos;s measurements. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
